WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.930
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.020 --> 01:39.800
Episode 20:
Soul Mate

01:43.990 --> 01:46.430
It was during the big market in Paris,

01:46.520 --> 01:51.610
that I met the Michelle family who were traveling performers from Lyons.

01:53.430 --> 01:58.800
It seemed like Michelle’s only daughter, Cosette, hated me at first.

01:59.460 --> 02:00.680
It's none of your business.

02:01.420 --> 02:02.640
Cosette...

02:03.190 --> 02:06.400
And then Mattia talked to Cosette.

02:06.670 --> 02:11.760
Mr. Vitalis told her "Remy, you're a cheerful girl."

02:12.310 --> 02:17.800
"Don't lose it. Cheerfulness is strength and hope."

02:18.280 --> 02:22.160
But you can't survive in Paris with that optimistic mind.

02:22.560 --> 02:27.840
But she still follows it earnestly, believes in it...

02:28.200 --> 02:30.960
Even when she wants to cry during hard times.

02:31.180 --> 02:32.760
That's Remy.

02:34.570 --> 02:36.840
We're friends.

02:37.040 --> 02:40.300
Friends?
- Yup. We're friends already.

02:40.860 --> 02:41.980
Remy...

02:43.940 --> 02:46.610
Thank you. Thank you, Remy.

03:01.970 --> 03:03.540
Now, audience.

03:03.620 --> 03:09.090
Our next performance is a singing act, starring Cosette and Remy.

03:14.070 --> 03:18.110
Remy, I have a favor to ask you.
- What?

03:19.140 --> 03:21.300
I'd like you to go shopping with me.

03:21.500 --> 03:25.360
Shopping?
- Tomorrow is my mother's birthday.

03:25.450 --> 03:27.600
I'm thinking about buying her a present.

03:28.050 --> 03:30.450
This is my pocket money.

03:30.600 --> 03:34.950
I have 12 sous. I've been saving it for a long time.

03:35.120 --> 03:37.770
I was planning to buy something for me.

03:38.970 --> 03:44.580
But I changed my mind. It'd be better if I spend it on my mother.

03:45.440 --> 03:47.710
Great! That's great, Cosette.

03:49.370 --> 03:54.960
But I don't know what to buy, so I want you to come with me.

03:55.250 --> 03:57.470
I understand. We'll go tomorrow.

03:58.580 --> 03:59.350
I'm so glad.

03:59.700 --> 04:02.340
Cosette! It's almost time for dinner.

04:03.050 --> 04:06.050
Would you like to join us, Remy?
- Thank you very much.

04:06.130 --> 04:09.360
But I should really go home. Everyone is waiting for me.

04:09.550 --> 04:13.850
Oh they are... Then please take some candies for your friends.

04:14.330 --> 04:17.860
Wait one minute.
-  I will. Thank you very much.

04:24.760 --> 04:28.220
I'm home.
- Welcome back, Ricardo. You're early.

04:28.290 --> 04:31.110
Yeah, I earned a lot today.

04:31.350 --> 04:33.610
But this business trend will be over soon.

04:33.990 --> 04:37.430
The day after tomorrow, the market will be closed and everyone will be gone.

04:37.520 --> 04:39.630
The Michelle troupe too?
- Yeah.

04:40.010 --> 04:44.400
Remy will be disappointed.
She's become good friends with Cosette.

04:44.690 --> 04:46.120
It can't be helped.

04:46.160 --> 04:49.390
They have to go to the next town to perform or they won't make any money.

04:49.670 --> 04:53.960
Then...
Remy will go with Cosette, won't she?

04:54.360 --> 04:55.150
Why would she do that?

04:55.270 --> 04:59.030
Because recently Remy's always with Cosette.

04:59.100 --> 05:01.440
It's like she's forgotten about us.

05:01.460 --> 05:07.430
That's right... She might leave.
Remy used be a traveling entertainer.

05:07.560 --> 05:08.860
I don't want her to leave.

05:08.950 --> 05:11.990
Remy won't stay here forever.
- Huh?

05:12.160 --> 05:14.730
She's been looking for her mother.

05:14.730 --> 05:16.420
Right... Right...

05:16.870 --> 05:19.600
I don't... I don't want her to.

05:24.140 --> 05:28.200
Is dinner ready yet?
- It will be in a moment.

05:28.240 --> 05:30.530
Do it quickly!
- Yes!

05:32.040 --> 05:34.020
Yesterday's candy was delicious, wasn't it?

05:34.210 --> 05:35.160
It was.

05:35.180 --> 05:38.020
It's good that Remy became friends with Cosette.

05:38.950 --> 05:40.520
Good morning!

05:40.690 --> 05:44.090
Wait, Remy!
Let's go to the market together!

05:44.150 --> 05:48.320
Sorry, I have something important to do! I need to leave early!

05:52.340 --> 05:54.740
There she goes again, running off with Cosette.

05:55.110 --> 05:57.510
She does that every day now.

06:05.380 --> 06:08.070
Mother, can I go out with Remy for a little while?

06:08.250 --> 06:11.090
Just be back by the afternoon performance.
- Yup.

06:15.100 --> 06:16.560
Hey.
- Eh?

06:16.860 --> 06:19.820
Shine my shoes.
- Oh, yes.

06:19.970 --> 06:25.240
Wow... What a beautiful hat.
- That hat would look nice on my mother.

06:25.240 --> 06:28.830
It does look nice.
- You think so? Then I'll buy it.

06:32.120 --> 06:33.310
Wow?

06:33.440 --> 06:35.820
5 francs? It costs that much?

06:42.700 --> 06:45.080
You can find something cheaper over here.

06:45.300 --> 06:47.630
But I only have 12 sous.

06:47.720 --> 06:50.080
Don't give up, Cosette. Let's go.

06:53.410 --> 06:57.350
12 sous? You can't buy anything with that.

07:00.000 --> 07:02.970
Quit joking around.

07:04.280 --> 07:07.980
Handkerchiefs, would you like a handkerchief?

07:08.020 --> 07:11.480
Miss, I will give you a discount on this. How about 15 sous?

07:11.660 --> 07:15.030
Well...
- How about 12 sous?

07:15.580 --> 07:16.880
That's it!

07:20.100 --> 07:22.500
Wow, it's a beautiful handkerchief, isn't it?

07:22.720 --> 07:26.450
Will my mother like it?
- You could do some stitch work on it.

07:26.450 --> 07:26.860
Huh?

07:26.890 --> 07:31.010
You could stitch your mother's initials on the handkerchief.

07:31.830 --> 07:37.010
When I first found out that I was a foundling,

07:37.470 --> 07:43.510
I thought it would be great if my real mother was like mother Barberin in Chavanon.

07:44.320 --> 07:47.810
My mother in Chavanon village shared the same birthday with me.

07:48.690 --> 07:55.010
My mother gave me a hat, but I didn't know what to give her.

07:55.520 --> 07:57.920
So I sang a song for her as a present.

07:58.010 --> 08:01.540
A song?
- Yup, my mother was so happy.

08:02.090 --> 08:04.650
I love my mother very much.

08:07.050 --> 08:17.850
Mother, mother, my mother...

08:17.850 --> 08:21.180
Your gentle hugs holding me

08:21.550 --> 08:34.030
When I'm lonely and sleeping at night

08:35.330 --> 08:41.390
Her heart is my hometown

08:41.570 --> 08:47.980
My mother...

08:50.030 --> 08:54.790
I believe that my real mother has been looking out for me.

08:54.970 --> 08:58.960
If I meet my real mother, I'll never part from her.

09:00.410 --> 09:03.520
But, I don't know how to do stitching.

09:04.030 --> 09:07.420
We'll do it together.
- Are you good at stitching?

09:08.660 --> 09:12.140
Well... I've watched my mother Barberin do it.

09:12.890 --> 09:15.050
It'll be fine.
- Yup.

09:16.170 --> 09:19.020
All right. Keep moving forward.

09:19.700 --> 09:24.990
Phew... This is hard. It's not turning out like my mother's after all.

09:25.280 --> 09:28.760
But it seems interesting. Please teach me.
- Sure.

09:32.440 --> 09:37.420
Cosette...
- Woah! What? Mother! Don't scare me.

09:37.460 --> 09:42.360
What are you two doing? It makes me worried when you're so quiet.

09:42.380 --> 09:45.020
It's a secret.
A secret between me and Remy.

09:46.020 --> 09:49.700
I wonder what your secret is. I'd like to know it soon.

09:49.850 --> 09:53.250
That's enough.
Please go away, mother.

09:53.270 --> 09:56.860
You have a lot of things to do, don't you?
-Okay, okay...

09:56.950 --> 10:00.480
Could you give me a hint?
- Mother!

10:02.860 --> 10:05.280
Mother, happy birthday!

10:05.720 --> 10:09.450
This present is from me and Remy.
- Wow... I wonder what it is.

10:09.510 --> 10:11.710
Open it up, mother.
- Yes, yes.

10:15.440 --> 10:21.970
What a beautiful handkerchief.
- And your initials are stitched onto it.

10:22.190 --> 10:26.730
We did the stitching ourselves. Remy taught me.

10:27.120 --> 10:32.610
This is the first time I've ever received such a beautiful present, I'm so happy.

10:32.940 --> 10:35.740
Thank you! Thank you very much.

10:36.120 --> 10:39.990
Cosette, I'm glad you're my daughter.

10:40.350 --> 10:41.250
Mother...

10:42.880 --> 10:48.170
I'm sorry, mother. I've been so selfish.

10:48.220 --> 10:51.500
Cosette... My Cosette.

10:55.250 --> 10:58.050
Thank you, Remy.
- Ah...

11:19.320 --> 11:22.560
You're such a mischievous boy, aren't you?

11:23.200 --> 11:25.900
Cosette has become a cheerful girl, hasn't she?

11:25.920 --> 11:28.320
Yes, and it's all thanks to Remy.

11:28.940 --> 11:32.350
She won't want to leave Paris, though,

11:32.650 --> 11:35.390
since she's become friends with Remy.

11:35.410 --> 11:38.250
It can't be helped. She was born into a family of traveling entertainers.

11:38.320 --> 11:41.840
You're right.
But I still feel sorry for her.

11:42.150 --> 11:44.010
Well, I'm heading home.

11:44.510 --> 11:47.360
I don't want to be apart from you.
- Huh?

11:47.600 --> 11:51.610
We'll be returning to Lyons tomorrow.
So, I won't be able to see you, Remy.

11:51.980 --> 11:56.100
I want to be with you forever, Remy.
I don't want to say goodbye.

11:56.390 --> 11:58.350
Hey, Remy, let's go together.
- Huh?

11:58.600 --> 12:01.970
I've been thinking that it would be great if you'd become a member of our family.

12:01.990 --> 12:03.620
I can't do that.

12:03.950 --> 12:10.830
But Boss Gaspard is a cruel person. It's best that you leave him and live with us.

12:11.180 --> 12:14.070
You want to find your real mother, right?

12:14.140 --> 12:17.110
You won't be able to find her living in Gaspard's house.

12:17.120 --> 12:18.720
Remy, let's go, okay?

12:18.750 --> 12:20.840
We're friends, aren't we?

12:24.630 --> 12:26.080
<i>Mother...</i>

12:27.580 --> 12:32.120
Remy's been late recently.
What's she doing?

12:38.360 --> 12:40.230
Say something!

12:40.630 --> 12:43.690
She's with Cosette.
- Cosette?

12:43.710 --> 12:45.180
Who's that?

12:45.190 --> 12:46.760
She's the daughter of a family of traveling entertainers.

12:46.790 --> 12:48.630
Traveling entertainers?
- Yes.

12:48.650 --> 12:52.670
Remy has been working with the Michelle family troupe.

12:52.730 --> 12:56.150
She makes more money that way, so I guess she's thinking of working for them.

12:56.190 --> 12:59.410
What? Remy's going to run away?

12:59.410 --> 13:01.380
I didn't say that.

13:01.900 --> 13:02.880
Listen everyone!

13:03.690 --> 13:05.380
Don't even think about escaping!

13:05.760 --> 13:11.380
If even one of you escapes, you know what'll happen to the rest of you.

13:11.590 --> 13:13.910
Do you understand?
- Y-yes...

13:15.060 --> 13:18.410
She'll go with Cosette... For sure...

13:22.400 --> 13:25.900
I'm not saying I don't like Remy anymore.

13:26.080 --> 13:29.480
But when I see Remy with Cosette, it makes me upset.

13:30.860 --> 13:35.360
Cosette is lucky she has such a wonderful mother and father.

13:35.470 --> 13:39.160
Remy! Tomorrow!
That's a promise!

13:39.420 --> 13:41.600
Good night, Cosette.

13:44.860 --> 13:46.930
Remy was a foundling.

13:47.050 --> 13:49.880
But she had a good mother to raise her.

13:49.900 --> 13:52.470
And she might be able to find her real mother.

13:54.870 --> 13:58.110
I don't even know what my mother and father look like.

13:58.390 --> 14:02.050
All I can remember is being alone.

14:03.530 --> 14:06.330
So, I envy Remy and Cosette.

14:06.330 --> 14:10.210
I know I'm jealous, but I can't help it.

14:15.450 --> 14:18.340
I don't need my mother and father.

14:18.610 --> 14:21.850
I want my mother and father.

14:35.250 --> 14:37.940
Maria, you've changed.

14:39.260 --> 14:43.360
I've never seen you so upset.

14:43.470 --> 14:47.020
That's right.
- It's not just Maria.

14:47.190 --> 14:50.810
All of us have changed since we met Remy.

14:51.960 --> 14:52.790
Ricardo.

14:53.590 --> 14:55.680
Why did you stop stealing?

14:59.120 --> 15:03.330
What did you say to Lise?
- That stealing is not good.

15:03.680 --> 15:05.090
Remy is right.

15:05.290 --> 15:09.700
I've been thinking about
how bad stealing is.

15:09.760 --> 15:11.140
I don't want to do it anymore.

15:11.880 --> 15:15.890
Yes, since then I haven't stolen.

15:15.920 --> 15:17.630
Me either.

15:17.660 --> 15:21.670
Even though I get beaten by Gaspard, I won't steal.

15:21.950 --> 15:24.140
Remy has taught us so much.

15:24.570 --> 15:27.730
It wasn't Lise or Ricardo's fault that I got lost.

15:28.060 --> 15:31.610
It was my fault for forgetting how to get back.

15:32.490 --> 15:35.820
Mattia, don't lose hope.
Please don't give up.

15:36.460 --> 15:38.840
If you keep moving forward, you'll find the way to go.

15:41.310 --> 15:45.120
At that moment, I felt like I was hit hard.

15:46.550 --> 15:49.460
And then I saw the light.

15:54.950 --> 15:58.040
Perhaps, I might be able to find...

16:00.060 --> 16:01.450
...my own way.

16:17.100 --> 16:22.260
But I won't able to find anything if I stay here at Gaspard's place.

16:23.820 --> 16:25.590
There must be some solution.

16:26.980 --> 16:29.590
Mattia...
Are you thinking about escaping?

16:31.910 --> 16:36.830
But the boss just said...
- Are you planning to stay here forever?

16:38.330 --> 16:42.600
We've all lived taking our current lives for granted.

16:43.090 --> 16:44.700
But Remy's different.

16:44.700 --> 16:47.630
She always keeps moving forward.

16:48.310 --> 16:51.600
I want move forward like she does.

16:51.640 --> 16:56.870
So if we can get out of this place, then perhaps we could find our own lives.

16:57.920 --> 17:01.890
We could find our own lives...

17:02.110 --> 17:06.370
I'll encourage Remy.
I don't care if I get punished by the boss.

17:07.250 --> 17:08.130
Maria...

17:09.190 --> 17:11.630
All right, I'll do it with you.

17:12.100 --> 17:13.960
Me too.

17:15.930 --> 17:16.770
No!

17:18.000 --> 17:22.280
If Remy goes, then big brother Mattia will be gone, too!

17:22.730 --> 17:24.790
Everybody will be gone.

17:24.820 --> 17:25.920
I'll...

17:26.290 --> 17:28.020
I'll be all alone!

17:28.400 --> 17:29.980
I don't want to be alone.

17:43.440 --> 17:46.300
You want to find your real mother, right?

17:46.350 --> 17:49.540
You won't be able to find her living in Gaspard's house.

17:50.290 --> 17:53.530
Mr. Vitalis, what should I do?

17:59.660 --> 18:02.770
I'll be all alone.

18:02.970 --> 18:05.860
Lise, what's wrong? Lise?

18:07.620 --> 18:09.050
Did you have a bad dream?

18:13.020 --> 18:14.010
Remy...

18:14.500 --> 18:18.320
Don't worry about Lise.
Just think about yourself.

18:18.640 --> 18:20.540
We're ready.

18:24.130 --> 18:28.100
Remy escaped, you said?
You guys knew about it, didn't you?

18:59.880 --> 19:01.380
Mr. Vitalis...

19:02.860 --> 19:05.680
I'm sorry that I left you alone for so long.

19:06.400 --> 19:11.190
Today, the Michelle family is going back to Lyons, and they want me to come with them.

19:11.560 --> 19:15.150
I'm fine, so are Capi and Joli-Coeur...

19:15.600 --> 19:20.170
Mr. Vitalis, I've been thinking about going with Cosette.

19:20.330 --> 19:23.070
I don't think I'll be able to see my mother if I keep living this life.

19:23.090 --> 19:25.180
I want to find my mother.

19:25.340 --> 19:31.160
But I've only been thinking about myself.
I can't go and leave everyone behind.

19:31.420 --> 19:34.680
I can't leave the friends I've been living with behind.

19:35.060 --> 19:37.170
I love them.

19:37.260 --> 19:41.980
They're my friends.
Isn't that right, Mr. Vitalis?

19:44.050 --> 19:48.700
I'm sorry, Cosette. I'm sure we'll see each other during the market next year.

19:49.540 --> 19:51.630
I can't wait that long.

19:51.700 --> 19:54.960
A year passes quickly.
- You can't come no matter what, Remy?

19:56.460 --> 19:57.470
Right...

19:57.670 --> 20:00.470
Moving forward is looking towards tomorrow.

20:02.990 --> 20:03.980
Yes.

20:04.460 --> 20:06.400
Goodbye, Remy.

20:07.880 --> 20:10.020
Goodbye, Cosette.

20:13.370 --> 20:16.500
Sir, Madam, thank you so much for everything.

20:16.700 --> 20:18.460
Take care, Remy.

20:18.480 --> 20:22.010
If you get into trouble, please visit us in Lyons.

20:22.120 --> 20:25.000
I will! Thank you very much!

20:26.420 --> 20:30.050
Goodbye! Goodbye, Cosette!

20:30.980 --> 20:33.010
I'll see you again next year.

20:35.560 --> 20:40.520
No matter how far apart we are, we're friends, Cosette.

20:51.650 --> 20:55.030
Has Remy gone with Cosette like we feared?

21:01.900 --> 21:04.020
Come on guys, let's go home.

21:09.750 --> 21:11.340
Remy!

21:15.740 --> 21:25.000
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

21:15.810 --> 21:18.840
Remy, we thought you'd gone with Cosette.

21:19.620 --> 21:23.340
What? I wouldn't leave you behind.

21:25.160 --> 21:36.020
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

21:26.430 --> 21:28.040
Remy!

21:31.650 --> 21:32.610
Lise...

21:36.550 --> 21:46.430
Tomorrow's courage comes

21:46.490 --> 21:56.460
From the future that gives us our fate

21:56.460 --> 22:05.650
Try to look at them more

22:05.980 --> 22:09.750
You're beautiful now that

22:10.030 --> 22:22.000
Your eyes are filled with laughter

22:22.130 --> 22:32.010
Tomorrow I promise that

22:32.160 --> 22:41.930
There will always be mistakes but

22:42.060 --> 22:51.010
Try to seek for them more

22:51.650 --> 22:55.550
Give your heart to

22:55.590 --> 23:10.690
That person who is also seeking you

23:20.010 --> 23:20.880
He has a terrible fever.

23:22.490 --> 23:24.870
Remy, it's no use.

23:24.880 --> 23:27.240
There aren't any doctors who will come and see us.

23:27.260 --> 23:28.980
I won't give up.

23:31.420 --> 23:33.990
Can we not do anything for Marcel?

23:34.020 --> 23:37.520
<i>Violin of Memories</i>

23:34.020 --> 23:37.520
Next time:
